newcpu.c: trace the remaining non-JIT run loops

adm_cpu_trace_pre was hooked into m68k_run_1, 1_ce, 2ce, 2p and 2_020 only, so the CPU
trace came back silently EMPTY - not wrong, empty - in every configuration that selects
another loop. m68k_run_2_000 is the one that bites: it is what a 68000 with
cpu_compatible off ("Fastest possible") runs, reachable through a user .uae config.
m68k_run_3ce and m68k_run_3p cover 68040/68060.

Still untraced, deliberately: m68k_run_jit (a JIT block has no per-instruction dispatch
to hook) and m68k_run_mmu030/040/060 (MMU faults restart an instruction, so a hook there
would record it more than once).

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

diff --git a/sources/src/newcpu.c b/sources/src/newcpu.c
index e6aff05..3d5ddb4 100644
--- a/sources/src/newcpu.c
+++ b/sources/src/newcpu.c
@@ -6209,6 +6209,7 @@ static void m68k_run_3ce (void)
 					debug_trainer_match();
 				}
 #endif
+				adm_cpu_trace_pre(r);
 				(*cpufunctbl_noret[r->opcode])(r->opcode);
 
 				if (r->spcflags) {
@@ -6260,6 +6261,7 @@ static void m68k_run_3p(void)
 				}
 #endif
 
+				adm_cpu_trace_pre(r);
 				(*cpufunctbl_noret[r->opcode])(r->opcode);
 
 				cpu_cycles = 2 * CYCLE_UNIT;
@@ -6680,6 +6682,7 @@ static void m68k_run_2_000(void)
 				}
 #endif
 
+				adm_cpu_trace_pre(r);
 				cpu_cycles = (*cpufunctbl[r->opcode])(r->opcode) & 0xffff;
 				cpu_cycles = adjust_cycles (cpu_cycles);
 				do_cycles(cpu_cycles);
